---
source: crates/qrec-core/src/keymap/global.rs
expression: out
---
=== niri
binds {
    Mod+Shift+R { spawn "/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage" "record" "toggle"; }
    Mod+Shift+O { spawn "/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage" "record" "start" "--over-selection"; }
    Mod+Shift+D { spawn "/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage" "take" "discard-last"; }
}

=== sway
bindsym $mod+Shift+r exec /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle
bindsym $mod+Shift+o exec /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection
bindsym $mod+Shift+d exec /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last

=== i3
# i3's default config binds $mod+Shift+r to restart: remove that line.
bindsym $mod+Shift+r exec --no-startup-id /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle
bindsym $mod+Shift+o exec --no-startup-id /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection
bindsym $mod+Shift+d exec --no-startup-id /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last

=== hyprland
bind = SUPER SHIFT, R, exec, /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle
bind = SUPER SHIFT, O, exec, /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection
bind = SUPER SHIFT, D, exec, /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last

=== river
riverctl map normal Super+Shift R spawn '/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle'
riverctl map normal Super+Shift O spawn '/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection'
riverctl map normal Super+Shift D spawn '/home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last'

=== gnome
In GNOME Settings › Keyboard › View and Customize Shortcuts › Custom Shortcuts,
for each line choose Add Shortcut (or +), type its name and command, then set its shortcut.

Name               Command                                                                         Shortcut
Record toggle      /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle                  Super+Shift+R
Record over        /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection  Super+Shift+O
Discard last take  /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last              Super+Shift+D

=== kde
In System Settings › Keyboard › Shortcuts, for each line choose
Add New › Command or Script…, type its command, then set its shortcut.

Name               Command                                                                         Shortcut
Record toggle      /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record toggle                  Meta+Shift+R
Record over        /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage record start --over-selection  Meta+Shift+O
Discard last take  /home/me/Applications/Qrec-0.1.0-x86_64.AppImage take discard-last              Meta+Shift+D

